+# Full-update causal diagnostics
+
+Goal remains joint ready-task selection, replica placement/residence and gradient delivery within one optimizer update. The first33pilots are a negative result, not completion of that goal.
+
+Previous goal turn: progress (33processes, actual main-plan equality, numerical qualifications, independent artifacts). No live training is assumed; device admission is rechecked.
+
+This phase: isolate at final6e7dd58; build matching ABI1 original-Timer worker; qualify small anchor/B0/B1/B3 against fixed-home/Native FP32 gradients; collect at most3main-shape updates for fixed_home, anchor, B0, B1, B3 under same routing. Add explicit lifecycle producer/service/completion scopes to existing original-Timer capture, preserving rank-local clocks. No diagnostic wall time enters performance figures.
+
+Questions: (1) what fraction is actually MoE/replication-sensitive? (2) do CPU reads/object collectives drain the queue and destroy overlap? (3) where is dW service exposed, especially update-end? (4) are cached hits checkpoint-only or cross-microbatch?
+
+Fixed model remains L4 EP8 E256 K8 H4096 F1024 S16384 GA4/W2, recv262144, FP32 persistent/BF16 compute, <=90GiB. Small qualification L2 H512 F512 S256. Same owners, labels, seeds, logical routes and router scores. Ordinary branch only; shared expert stays framework.
+
+All remote operations use a new task directory/container/build/SOs and the shared device-jobs lock plus device ownership checks. No other job is stopped. Timed A/B source trees are read-only.
+
+Go/no-go: verify original Timer nonzero forward/replay/backward records and full-gradient thresholds before main capture; direct dependency edges and device-completed service marks before causal claims. Compare current rank-local intervals, never join independent device origins. Main capture requires a matching small qualification certificate, <=3updates, no multi-GiB gradient dump. Stop on numerical, stale source/SO, memory or ownership failure.
+
+Next research action follows evidence: remove redundant host observations only if they are exposed; test whether replication is worthwhile at stronger skew before spending on a joint device strategy. Do not treat simply beating a slow prototype as a contribution.
